 # Voxel Cone Tracing
 
-Also called: Approximate Voxel Cone Tracing, Cone Tracing Final Gathering, VCTGI, VXGI, Voxel Global Illumination, Voxel-based Global Illumination
+Also called: VCTGI, VXGI Cone Tracing, Voxel Global Illumination, Voxel-based Global Illumination
 
 ## Overview
-Voxel Cone Tracing (VCT) is a real-time global illumination technique that approximates indirect diffuse and specular lighting by voxelizing the scene geometry into a 3D texture or sparse octree and tracing cones through this volume to accumulate radiance [S1][S2, S6, unofficial]. It solves the problem of computing indirect light (interreflections) in dynamic scenes where precomputed methods are infeasible and full ray tracing is too slow [S1, S13]. Unlike [Spherical Harmonic Volumetric Visibility](1225-spherical-harmonic-volumetric-visibility.md) which encodes lighting in frequency domain, or [Precomputed Lighting (Baking)](2169-precomputed-lighting-baking.md) which requires static geometry, VCT operates on a spatially explicit voxel representation, allowing for dynamic objects and view-dependent effects like soft shadows and glossy reflections [S1, S13][S17, unofficial].
+Voxel Cone Tracing (VCT) is a real-time global illumination technique that approximates indirect diffuse and specular lighting by voxelizing scene geometry into a 3D texture or sparse octree and tracing cones through this volume to accumulate radiance [S1, unofficial][S2][S6, unofficial]. It solves the problem of computing indirect light (interreflections) in dynamic scenes where precomputed methods are infeasible and full ray tracing is too slow [S1, S13, unofficial]. Unlike [Spherical Harmonic Volumetric Visibility](1225-spherical-harmonic-volumetric-visibility.md) which encodes lighting in the frequency domain, or [Precomputed Lighting (Baking)](2169-precomputed-lighting-baking.md) which requires static geometry, VCT operates on a spatially explicit voxel representation, allowing for dynamic objects and view-dependent effects like soft shadows and glossy reflections [S1, S13, unofficial][S17, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-The method consists of three main phases: Voxelization (building the volume), Filtering (generating mipmaps for integration), and Cone Tracing (final gathering).
+The method consists of three main phases: Voxelization (building the volume), Filtering (generating mipmaps for integration), and Cone Tracing (final gathering) [S16, unofficial].
 
 ### Inputs and Outputs
-*   **Inputs:** Scene geometry (triangle meshes), camera position/view/projection matrices, light positions and intensities, material properties (albedo, normal, specular exponent/shininess).
-*   **Outputs:** Final pixel color containing direct lighting, indirect diffuse illumination, indirect specular/glossy reflections, and soft shadows.
+*   **Inputs:** Scene geometry (triangle meshes), camera position/view/projection matrices, light positions and intensities, material properties (albedo, normal, specular exponent/shininess) [S2, S14][G].
